The two spheres intersect when the distance between their centers is between the difference and sum of their radii. In this case, $3\sqrt{5}=D-(5\sqrt5-2\sqrt17)<D<D+(5\sqrt5-2\sqrt17)=9\sqrt5$, so the spheres intersect. When the spheres intersect, they form a circle whose radius $r$ can be found using the formula $r=\sqrt{R^2-d^2/4}$, where $R$ is the radius of the sphere that is farther from the circle, $d$ is the distance between the centers of the spheres, and $r$ is the radius of the circle. In this case, $R=2\sqrt17$ and $d=9$, so \begin{align*}r&=\sqrt{\left(2\sqrt{17}\right)^2-\left(\frac{9}{2}\right)^2}\\&=\sqrt{68-\frac{81}{4}}\\&=\sqrt{\frac{163}{4}}\\&=\boxed{\frac{\sqrt{163}}{2}}\end{align*}
